<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'none'; img-src 'none'; font-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; frame-src 'none'; worker-src 'none'; media-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'">
  <title>S095 · Required candidate dependency partition</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
  <script src="model.js" defer></script>
  <script src="app.js" defer></script>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#exercise">Skip to rehearsal controls</a>
  <header>
    <p class="banner" id="training-banner">Training rehearsal - synthetic data - not a live Azure result</p>
    <p class="identity">A-S095 · D-S095 · SC-S095 · frozen Kano S · synthetic fixture s095-v1</p>
    <h1>Required candidate dependency partition</h1>
    <p>Partition a required candidate dependency; identify safe versus unsafe admission decisions.</p>
    <p><strong>Exact S095 requirement:</strong> Remove it from new admission and retain a usable compatible destination.</p>
  </header>
  <main>
    <section aria-labelledby="envelope-title">
      <h2 id="envelope-title">Fixed teaching envelope</h2>
      <p>One fictional required service path on <strong>candidate-v2, epoch 2</strong> is partitioned.
        <strong>old-v1, epoch 1</strong> is the retained destination; the fixture determines its observed compatibility.
        No optional or shared dependency is disabled. Last-known 50/50 eligibility is not fresh readiness evidence after the fault.</p>
      <p>Each independent replay has <strong>four new arrivals</strong>, a <strong>250 ms original complete-journey budget</strong>,
        preserved session and saved state, and exactly one required effect. Two later candidate recovery
        <strong>validation probes are not user migrations</strong>. All faults, gates, routing, repair and admission instructions
        below are fixed trace data, never networking or resource operations.</p>
    </section>
    <section id="exercise" aria-labelledby="controls-title">
      <h2 id="controls-title">Operate the synthetic rehearsal</h2>
      <p id="instructions">Choose observed conditions, an admission instruction and your predicted <em>source safety result</em>.
        Rehearse and inspect measured facts. Correctly predicting failure is a learning pass, not successful service.
        Six attempts remain visible; a seventh is rejected until explicit reset.</p>
      <form id="rehearsal-form" aria-describedby="instructions">
        <div class="control">
          <label for="fixture">Observation fixture</label>
          <select id="fixture" name="fixture">
            <option value="healthy-survivor">Observed healthy + compatible survivor</option>
            <option value="incompatible-survivor">Healthy HTTP 200, incompatible saved state</option>
            <option value="missing-evidence">Missing gate / routing / client / recovery observations</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="control">
          <label for="admission-action">Admission instruction (teaching data only)</label>
          <select id="admission-action" name="action">
            <option value="gate-candidate">Remove candidate admission; wait for fresh recovery proof</option>
            <option value="keep-candidate">Keep candidate admitting during the partition (unsafe)</option>
            <option value="reopen-unverified">Remove, then reopen before recovery proof (unsafe)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="control">
          <label for="prediction">Predicted source safety acceptance</label>
          <select id="prediction" name="prediction">
            <option value="success">Success — safe containment with retained compatible service and recovery evidence</option>
            <option value="failure">Failure — unsafe admission or unusable survivor</option>
            <option value="unknown">Unknown — missing observations cannot establish acceptance</option>
          </select>
        </div>
        <div class="buttons">
          <button id="run-rehearsal" type="submit">Rehearse and check</button>
          <button id="reset-rehearsal" type="button">Reset rehearsal</button>
        </div>
      </form>
      <p id="input-error" class="error" role="alert" tabindex="-1" hidden></p>
      <p id="run-status" role="status" aria-live="polite">No attempts yet. Choose conditions and rehearse.</p>
      <noscript>This local exercise requires JavaScript. No rehearsal result has been observed.</noscript>
    </section>
    <section id="result" aria-labelledby="result-title" hidden>
      <h2 id="result-title" tabindex="-1">Latest synthetic observation</h2>
      <p id="source-result" class="verdict"></p>
      <p id="learning-result"></p>
      <p id="explanation"></p>
      <p id="instruction-assessment"></p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table aria-label="Exact source acceptance assertions">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Source assertion</th><th scope="col">Observed result</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="assertion-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Partition, retained service and recovery facts</h3>
      <dl id="facts"></dl>
      <h3>Four ordinary arrivals during the partition</h3>
      <p>Candidate-intended arrivals are transition trials; unknown trials remain counted.
        Arrivals entirely on old-v1 do not establish migration. Every fact below is synthetic.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table aria-label="Synthetic partition journey observations">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Journey</th><th scope="col">Intended → observed / epoch</th><th scope="col">HTTP / ms</th><th scope="col">Session / state / effects</th><th scope="col">Outcome and reason</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="journey-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Recovery validation — separate, not migration credit</h3>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table aria-label="Synthetic recovery validation probes">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Probe</th><th scope="col">Intended → observed / epoch</th><th scope="col">HTTP / ms</th><th scope="col">Session / state / effects</th><th scope="col">Outcome and reason</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="recovery-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h3>Retained synthetic trace</h3>
      <ol id="trace"></ol>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="history-title">
      <h2 id="history-title">Retained attempt history</h2>
      <p id="summary">0 / 6 attempts. Safety: 0 success, 0 failure, 0 unknown. Journeys: 0 success, 0 interruption, 0 unknown. No transition evidence.</p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table aria-label="Retained synthetic attempt ledger">
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Attempt</th><th scope="col">Fixture and instruction</th><th scope="col">Source safety / prediction</th><th scope="col">Learning</th><th scope="col">Journey success / interruption / unknown</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody id="history-rows"></tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>Control changes and later successful recovery do not remove older failure or unknown rows.
        History is bounded, memory-only and cleared only by explicit reset or reload. Reset creates no resource cleanup claim.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="limits-title">
      <h2 id="limits-title">Boundary and keyboard help</h2>
      <p>Use Tab, select arrow keys and Enter/Space. Errors are announced and focused.
        Reset restores all default controls, clears results/errors/history/counters and focuses the fixture selector.</p>
      <p>This standalone bundle illustrates required-dependency admission gating. It does not certify any supported Azure
        mechanism, actual dependency partition, routing, admission, recovery, native B-S095, D-S022/D-S095 completion,
        production Node.js 24, statistical independence or five-nines reliability. An empty transition sample is not 100% success.</p>
      <p>No server, storage, cloud, IaC, scaffold, framework, account, identity, credentials, management calls,
        resource operations, deployment or spend. CSP denies connections, inline execution and form navigation.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
  <footer>
    <h2>Microsoft Open Source Disclaimer</h2>
    <p>The examples and guidance in this repository are provided "AS IS" for educational and demonstration purposes, without warranties or guarantees, express or implied, except as otherwise required by applicable law or binding terms. Validate their security, reliability, compatibility, and cost implications before production use.</p>
    <p>References to Microsoft, Azure, and other Microsoft products or services are for identification and illustration only. They do not imply endorsement, sponsorship, certification, or support by Microsoft. The 99.999% transition-success target is a project goal, not a Microsoft service-level agreement or guarantee.</p>
    <p>Microsoft and Azure are trademarks of the Microsoft group of companies. Other trademarks are the property of their respective owners.</p>
  </footer>
</body>
</html>
